+Why: the branch joins quoted lines, but it still splits on `\n` and never strips the `\r`, so the issue's own repro (CRLF export, `newline=''`) returns the note as `call back\r\nafter 5pm"\r` instead of `call back\r\nafter 5pm`. A stray closing quote and a trailing `\r` also corrupt every quoted field (`note\r`, `no notes"\r`). The new test uses LF-only input, never the reported `\r\n`, and its second assertion expects `"x, y"` to split into `x` and ` y`, codifying incorrect quoted-comma handling rather than checking the fix. Suite passes, but it cannot detect the CRLF failure the issue describes.
